'''Gemstones''' are a category of {{Skl|Mining}} [[Collection]] items. They can be applied to items with [[Gemstone Slot]]s to grant stat boosts, and are used in a variety of crafting and [[Forging]] recipes.
== Collection ==
Collecting all types of '''Gemstones''' will contribute to the '''Gemstone''' [[Collection]], rather than having each individual '''Gemstone''' having its own unique collection.
{{/Collection UI}}
{{CollectionTable|Gemstone}}

== Mechanics ==
Gemstones come in {{Green|12}} varieties: {{Item|Ruby}}, {{Item|Amber}}, {{Item|Sapphire}}, {{Item|Jade}}, {{Item|Amethyst}}, {{Item|Topaz}}, {{Item|Jasper}}, {{Item|Opal}}, {{Item|Onyx}}, {{Item|Aquamarine}}, {{Item|Citrine}} and {{Item|Peridot}}.

Each '''Gemstone''' has {{Green|5}} tiers, listed from lowest to highest: Rough, {{green|Flawed}}, {{blue|Fine}}, {{purple|Flawless}} and {{gold|Perfect}}. Each tier is crafted from {{Green|80}} of the previous, with the exception of {{orange|Perfect}}, which is forged with {{Green|5}} {{purple|Flawless}} '''Gemstones''' and their respective [[Gemstone Crystal]].

{{:Gemstone/Stats}}

== Obtaining ==
=== Mining ===
[[File:Mithril Deposits Jade.png|thumb|300px|Jade Gemstones in the {{Zone|Mithril Deposits}}]]
'''Gemstones''' can be mined all around the {{Zone|Crystal Hollows}}, {{Zone|Smoldering Tomb}}, {{Zone|Glacite Tunnels}} and {{Zone|Glacite Mineshafts}}.

Mining '''Gemstones''' will drop {{green|3-5}} of the Rough tier by default. {{Stat|Pristine}} grants a chance to replace the Rough '''Gemstone''' drops with {{green|Flawed}} '''Gemstones'''.

